  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The mixture of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math> is known water gas as it is used in the synthesis of other compounds.</p><p>When carbon monoxide reacts with hydrogen in presence of catalyst cobalt&nbsp;the product formed is&nbsp;methanol. Therefore, water gas is producing a an alcohol in this reaction.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/6803a5b7-299e-41c6-9ec2-3050566c05b1-image.png\" style=\"width: 481px; height: 131px;\" /></p>",
